            "rubricHtml": "<p>Questions 31–34</p>",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the sentences below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><p>American Salt Marshes</p><ul><li><strong>31</strong> &nbsp;The salt content in marshes can be as high as that of the {{31}}.</li><li><strong>32</strong> &nbsp;At different times of the day, there are changes in salinity and in the {{32}} and warmth of the water.</li><li><strong>33</strong> &nbsp;Animals such as worms and shrimps feed on the {{33}} that grow in the marsh.</li><li><strong>34</strong> &nbsp;Marshland in the US has been used in the past for {{34}} cultivation.</li></ul>",
            "maxWords": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "part-4-group-2",
            "type": "mcq",
            "rubricHtml": "<p>Questions 35–38</p>",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 35,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;The speaker says that one result of erecting artificial walls in salt marshes is that",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "water levels can get too high."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "wildlife has less space."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "water quality is difficult to control."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 36,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;Some people have complained about the building of dikes because",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "access for walkers is reduced"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "the insect population has increased."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "the natural beauty of the area is affected"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 37,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;In the 20th century, a large proportion of marshes in America became",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "salt extraction sites."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "residential areas."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "protected insect reserves."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 38,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;There are now laws which help to prevent",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "the erosion of soil"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "the building of more walls."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "the extinction of sealife"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
